(Vox OS Core Utilities)
A text called "Program Version" is "0.1.10".

(Parse the flags now)
A flag called "wants help" is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called "wants version" is "--version" or "-v", it is a boolean.
A text called "Program" is arguments's name.

If "wants help" then,
  Print "{Program} - unmount filesystems",
  Print "Usage: {Program} [OPTION]... TARGET...",
  Print "With no TARGET, or when TARGET is -, read standard input.",
  Print "\nOptions:",
  Print "  -h, --help   display this help and exit",
  Print "  -v, --version output version information and exit",
  Print "\nExamples:",
  Print "\t{Program} /dev/sda1 /mnt\tUnmount /dev/sda1 from /mnt",
  Print "\t{Program} - /mnt\tUnmount /dev/sda1 (assumed) from /mnt",
  Print "See https://github.com/vox-lang/vox for more information.",
  Exit 0.
  
Open a file for writing at "/dev/stderr" called stderr.

To 'unmount target' with a text called 'target path'.
    Unmount 'target path'.
      On error write "{Program}: Failed to unmount {target path}\n" to stderr.

"unmount target" on each target from arguments's all.
